aration / 2b origin trust / 2c shape: unavailable means nothing was declared and is produced only by 2a; untrusted means something was declared and is unusable, including a declared root that does not exist. The cut is declaration presence, not severity, and it matches the existing guidance classes (host vs configuration).\n\n(3) Payload representable. New 5.1: a discriminated union whose shape is derived, not chosen - a code carries exactly the values established where it fires, and the stage steps are totally ordered, so shape is a function of the code. effective_requirement absent in exactly two codes, resolved_version and prerelease absent in exactly five. requirement_invalid carries source_ref plus a closed violation token and must not echo the offending value (no unvalidated package byte in a payload); requirement_unsatisfiable carries the individually validated fragments plus the max-lower and min-upper bounds with every source achieving each in fixed order, so the payload is as source-order-independent as the intersection.\n\n(4) Catalog unambiguous. Coverage is defined by the selection function: any, per_os and hybrid are all valid, and the gate checks resolution (every registry OS resolves to exactly one active entry) plus reachability (an exact entry for an OS outside the registry, or an any entry shadowed everywhere, fails). New 6.2.1 states append-only against the catalog version: a published version is immutable in whole, every change is an N to N+1 transition, the entry set only grows, active and superseded_by are one-way monotone, and four transitions are admissible including retire-without-successor only for a tuple the gate no longer requires. Exactly-one-active-per-tuple relaxes to at-most-one.\n\nVector inventory 58 -\u003e 95 cases: Go classifier positives 9/10/12/13/14 and negatives 45-54 including class boundary 47 and value-class precedence 54; overlap vectors 24-28 and 33-34; payload-shape vectors 65-71; catalog coverage 79-84 and version tr