.task-board/.resources/TASK-260729-1kq1rd/TASK-260729-1kq1rd_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-f4b349.log:5228:EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/progress.md:95:Implemented portable manager-worker-v1 go-v1 pipeline in internal/godriver against the accepted rc.5 candidate (manifest sha256:58f8d229..., vector sha256:c3d42f76...). Added: execution_policy=manager-worker-v1 in buildmeta (portable cache key reproduces sha256:529370122ae1... exactly); rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 probe + closed capability-evidence-v1 record with the eight consistency rules; identity-verified hidden-mode worker (cmd/curator __curator-go-worker-v1) with nonce-bound list/validate/HMAC-permit/build state machine; native macOS controls (setsid session teardown, RLIMIT_FSIZE, close-on-exec descriptor release) and Windows Job Object controls (kill-on-close, active-process, job/process memory, explicit handle inheritance list); parent-enforced domain deadline/output/artifact bounds; pre/post worker, source-snapshot and toolchain identity checks; package-influence guard over the closed build-command surface. Removed the decorative HostPolicy adapter that the previous review rejected. macOS gates green: go build, go vet, go test ./..., go test -race ./..., gofmt, rc.5 conformance, real Go 1.25.5 vendored build. Native Windows validation running over ssh win with Go 1.25.5 windows/amd64. Linux runtime deferred: rc5-native-control-inventory-v1 covers only macOS and Windows, so Linux rejects with build_execution_control_unavailable before the worker; compile and unit coverage only.
